values ('a3b4c5d6-7e8f-4a71-8c01-1d2e3f4a5b81', 'ux-user-experience-design', 'UX / User Experience Design', 'UX / User Experience Design is an upper-division Graphic Design elective focused on user research, information architecture, interaction design, prototyping, usability, accessibility, design systems, and portfolio-ready UX case studies. The course is calibrated for students moving from visual communication into product, service, interface, and human-centered design. It treats UX as evidence-driven design practice: students investigate people and contexts, model systems, prototype alternatives, test with users, revise from evidence, and communicate decisions to collaborators.');

