  'UX / User Experience Design',
  'UX / User Experience Design is an upper-division Graphic Design elective focused on user research, information architecture, interaction design, prototyping, usability, accessibility, design systems, and portfolio-ready UX case studies. The course is calibrated for students moving from visual communication into product, service, interface, and human-centered design. It treats UX as evidence-driven design practice: students investigate people and contexts, model systems, prototype alternatives, test with users, revise from evidence, and communicate decisions to collaborators.',
  $uxdsjson${"slug": "ux-user-experience-design", "title": "UX / User Experience Design", "description": "UX / User Experience Design is an upper-division Graphic Design elective focused on user research, information architecture, interaction design, prototyping, usability, accessibility, design systems, and portfolio-ready UX case studies. The course is calibrated for students moving from visual communication into product, service, interface, and human-centered design. It treats UX as evidence-driven design practice: students investigate people and contexts, model systems, prototype alternatives, test with users, revise from evidence, and communicate decisions to collaborators.", "topics": [{"id": "b58abda4-6df0-45cb-bb8c-d2a7e5e364fe", "type": "topic", "title": "UX Foundations and Human-Centered Design", "description": "This opening section gives students the map of the field: UX as the design of useful, usable, accessible, credible, and meaningful experiences across products and services.", "children": [{"id": "388da59d-4bf5-4f6f-a9c5-3435cb48fccb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "What UX includes", "children": [{"id": "2d2962f9-a300-4eec-a912-6e206f7c4775", "type": "concept", "title": "User needs and business goals"}, {"id": "8dddd068-bdf1-42c2-a930-f885c0e6ff35", "type": "concept", "title": "Usability, usefulness, desirability, and accessibility"}, {"id": "2b48cefa-7f05-4f9c-819d-d4d9d47447b7", "type": "concept", "title": "UX roles and deliverables"}], "description": "Students learn the boundaries and overlaps among UX, UI, product design, HCI, service design, and visual communication."}, {"id": "73d1ecab-87ab-4ab9-ba6a-248c77cd2cdd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Human-centered mindset", "children": [{"id": "0087219b-a873-456d-8536-9eb720960064", "type": "concept", "title": "Empathy and evidence"}, {"id": "209f80b7-6b66-4245-96e0-cee4f153dcd8", "type": "concept", "title": "Context of use"}, {"id": "720a71ef-4b2c-4e2f-bbf2-caaf4ac70834", "type": "concept", "title": "Iteration and humility"}], "description": "The point is to start with people and context before jumping into screens."}, {"id": "4dc05e6e-0f84-4d83-a84b-9e0af5a0f40d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "UX vocabulary", "children": [{"id": "3726b4f3-f4d1-4177-a1c4-9c6f0d9d4e6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Flows, tasks, journeys, IA, wireframes"}, {"id": "ae0e5330-a8b0-4ee5-8475-88e83aaea3ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Prototype fidelity"}, {"id": "54e9c7da-270d-417c-b2f5-4a9824a012c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Heuristics and affordances"}], "description": "Shared language makes critique and collaboration sharper."}]}, {"id": "33dbb778-8f54-4721-ac84-90b1155c57d4", "type": "topic", "title": "Problem Framing, Stakeholders, and Product Strategy", "description": "Strong UX begins with the right problem. Students learn to define scope, constraints, stakeholder goals, product assumptions, and decision criteria before designing.", "children": [{"id": "b929d473-055f-4dcf-abf1-4516aae66c85", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Problem statements", "children": [{"id": "e7a3e178-c046-48b2-aea4-3c8ab14d25f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Problem framing"}, {"id": "307f5535-0604-4346-bed0-a7f476424984", "type": "concept", "title": "Opportunity statements"}, {"id": "2b56f37d-d782-4f35-b1ec-111b34cc1e27", "type": "concept", "title": "Assumptions and risks"}], "description": "Students turn vague briefs into focused design challenges."}, {"id": "0184fdc8-95ee-4d91-a5b8-33eb54ab8928", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Stakeholder mapping", "children": [{"id": "071dcaf3-6c55-4db0-8898-216aadde231f", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary and secondary stakeholders"}, {"id": "512aef46-c44b-4ce6-8b70-4f1ae9c225b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Power and interest mapping"}, {"id": "a75eca56-a8d4-4f39-b73c-ae79a157010f", "type": "concept", "title": "Conflicting goals"}], "description": "The gist is to understand who influences, funds, builds, uses, and is affected by the product."}, {"id": "f3d4b5f6-aa94-404e-9318-a3b11f8efbda", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Product success criteria", "children": [{"id": "7b04db01-d55e-4051-9b37-323b477e7c12", "type": "concept", "title": "User outcomes"}, {"id": "bfd915f4-4169-4d4b-a4be-84debb112e59", "type": "concept", "title": "Business or mission outcomes"}, {"id": "18a1d0da-f61d-4246-ba17-91950d4312d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Technical and operational constraints"}], "description": "Students connect design work to measurable and meaningful outcomes."}]}, {"id": "53be7c49-da85-403c-9f4f-8c5aee2eb214", "type": "topic", "title": "User Research Planning and Ethics", "description": "This section teaches students to plan research responsibly. The emphasis is on asking answerable questions, recruiting appropriately, and protecting participants.", "children": [{"id": "8a1d79f7-0d02-4044-b73d-25a2c053bc18", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research questions", "children": [{"id": "4b28aff5-5406-4199-a604-0af89707fdaf", "type": "concept", "title": "Generative versus evaluative research"}, {"id": "21ea05e9-f46b-4924-b5a6-e24330142436", "type": "concept", "title": "Behavior versus attitude"}, {"id": "e144b1ae-b3e6-4484-9847-9c19a5d7be01", "type": "concept", "title": "Scope and feasibility"}], "description": "Students learn to choose methods based on what they need to learn."}, {"id": "c3e41e87-27c2-4490-948f-21a5653c09fa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sampling and recruiting", "children": [{"id": "1f5832ab-aa11-4622-ab06-6b412ac78363", "type": "concept", "title": "Participant criteria"}, {"id": "6c3e7afb-b880-48d0-a7f7-e0145dae3c3c", "type": "concept", "title": "Screeners and incentives"}, {"id": "fa64c8fd-47f5-4f20-9972-7efd4577e158", "type": "concept", "title": "Recruiting bias"}], "description": "The point is to hear from relevant participants without pretending small samples represent everyone."}, {"id": "768846ad-b923-49d7-ab2c-d66daf7a7c38", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethics and consent", "children": [{"id": "10e6976c-fc09-4f49-aff3-66fee23adf05", "type": "concept", "title": "Informed consent"}, {"id": "1653d898-8e5d-4ea6-a757-67a70c94f3ed", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy and data minimization"}, {"id": "48f5d252-4af0-4947-878f-d1cda27a5ea9", "type": "concept", "title": "Power, vulnerability, and inclusion"}], "description": "Students learn to respect participants and handle data carefully."}]}, {"id": "b3d6bb79-736d-4598-b27b-ec59a7cf8ede", "type": "topic", "title": "Qualitative Research: Interviews, Observation, and Fieldwork", "description": "Qualitative research helps designers understand context, motivations, pain points, and workarounds. Students practice asking, watching, listening, and documenting.", "children": [{"id": "eb8cfd0c-786e-4b96-bfde-e96402dfb6ca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interviewing", "children": [{"id": "fa324e32-761c-43ee-9881-50a1b3c0c6fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Interview guides"}, {"id": "50106bfe-e0a9-45ad-92a8-6e56b63422ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Probing and silence"}, {"id": "0bd18e28-bc7e-4e16-975a-7c8c2a80ad53", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding confirmation bias"}], "description": "Students learn to ask open, non-leading questions and follow the participant's reality."}, {"id": "e0844056-51a1-4125-8150-e401e0d85b6d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Observation and contextual inquiry", "children": [{"id": "0d893067-9517-4da2-887b-4c9266ba2f64", "type": "concept", "title": "Context of use"}, {"id": "301c2743-771e-415a-b09b-8d2be61aff00", "type": "concept", "title": "Workarounds and breakdowns"}, {"id": "78f9b919-ae73-42ed-beba-fdb3de200de1", "type": "concept", "title": "Artifacts and environments"}], "description": "The gist is to study what people do, not only what they say."}, {"id": "9be9e50d-2834-472a-b7e2-f13d77ef9836", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research notes", "children": [{"id": "9899b893-b4e0-44ac-a365-3dbfd3043632", "type": "concept", "title": "Note-taking roles"}, {"id": "8d398992-8e89-464b-81ce-b12b4ce76b9b", "type": "concept", "title": "Quotes and observations"}, {"id": "68f7ec18-531a-43f7-a62a-a10cfc609f9f", "type": "concept", "title": "Debriefs and research repositories"}], "description": "Students learn to capture evidence in a way that supports later synthesis."}]}, {"id": "a35d1e49-b6d0-477d-ac4e-7a5db95d2059", "type": "topic", "title": "Quantitative UX, Surveys, Analytics, and Evidence", "description": "Quantitative evidence helps students see patterns at scale. This topic teaches them to use numbers carefully, avoiding false precision and vanity metrics.", "children": [{"id": "aa990759-ea01-41a0-81e3-49fed84422d4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Survey basics", "children": [{"id": "9dd9f83c-00a7-4658-a99b-19dda2102ffb", "type": "concept", "title": "Question design"}, {"id": "82d00a82-b331-473d-9021-9dc5e8461ab6", "type": "concept", "title": "Scales and response options"}, {"id": "ae534dd3-145e-45ee-84c7-45243e3a4115", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling limits"}], "description": "Students learn when surveys help and how poor wording can ruin results."}, {"id": "508b48ca-9a3b-4ce1-bbdf-14966731132b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Analytics and behavioral data", "children": [{"id": "498a46ed-f062-4f27-aeb3-5c9a75be0227", "type": "concept", "title": "Funnels and drop-off"}, {"id": "15f01a5f-9883-4ea0-b35c-4288b5f0d9f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Search terms and click paths"}, {"id": "7d7a038b-5a19-49c6-974e-9c179de81c3c", "type": "concept", "title": "Cohorts and segments"}], "description": "The point is to interpret product behavior without forgetting user intent."}, {"id": "a50b3d8d-3747-4d2f-91ab-9c3bfaa8bfac", "type": "subtopic", "title": "UX metrics", "children": [{"id": "8df1c83b-6395-4041-8fd2-37e0ef4b36bf", "type": "concept", "title": "Task success and time on task"}, {"id": "1c241e4e-64ad-42c8-a5d2-9101cbff5176", "type": "concept", "title": "Satisfaction and confidence"}, {"id": "2bab7537-1436-4d70-a083-72612cb1017e", "type": "concept", "title": "Retention, conversion, and error rates"}], "description": "Students choose metrics that match the research question."}]}, {"id": "755780cb-b0b0-41bc-8e23-4ee2013342b4", "type": "topic", "title": "Synthesis: Personas, Journey Maps, Jobs, and Service Blueprints", "description": "Synthesis turns raw evidence into shared understanding. Students learn to model users, goals, tasks, pain points, and service systems without flattening real people into stereotypes.", "children": [{"id": "c6d790cc-ff80-40c1-a272-2020985013c6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Affinity mapping", "children": [{"id": "cfd7861e-99e8-4a8b-9d0e-48aba3b1fda9", "type": "concept", "title": "Clustering notes"}, {"id": "5004cd9e-9b67-47e3-a510-f3c85f5f4722", "type": "concept", "title": "Theme naming"}, {"id": "c3d1ad08-f62b-4889-b401-20e1ec829e42", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence-backed insights"}], "description": "Students organize observations into patterns and themes."}, {"id": "3a7cc21f-5472-479b-8674-1d3d3fb2cef2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Personas and jobs", "children": [{"id": "05fcbc4d-0016-4e33-bf4e-c88045b7b9c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Behavioral personas"}, {"id": "0f783453-3011-4ee5-b2b9-fee7b94d9b60", "type": "concept", "title": "Jobs-to-be-done"}, {"id": "186a4dd4-4573-4637-b452-ba55e5e19b4e", "type": "concept", "title": "Anti-personas and edge cases"}], "description": "The gist is to represent motivations and goals in useful design models."}, {"id": "90827203-b855-45dc-b936-1561b5ef2da9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Journey and service maps", "children": [{"id": "2c8c8a4a-7458-43b6-81ec-a522ae7d7a6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Journey stages"}, {"id": "fe20aab1-8f32-4e27-86a0-9bf14a71bd73", "type": "concept", "title": "Pain points and moments of truth"}, {"id": "7e060dd1-df1e-4006-a2b9-df51213fd70e", "type": "concept", "title": "Service blueprint frontstage/backstage"}], "description": "Students map experiences across time, channels, emotions, and backstage systems."}]}, {"id": "89813bb6-eec5-40ec-837c-1d140df2fa7c", "type": "topic", "title": "Information Architecture, Taxonomy, Navigation, and Labeling", "description": "Information architecture helps people find and understand what they need. Students learn to structure content and navigation based on mental models and evidence.", "children": [{"id": "6f13aa80-5c8c-46c5-a165-9e79e42dcd49", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Content inventory and audit", "children": [{"id": "50e1a324-0330-4243-b351-41e4235e609f", "type": "concept", "title": "Content types and owners"}, {"id": "fc55e756-9bc4-4d86-b9b8-f453a143b4e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Redundancy and gaps"}, {"id": "4fca3a9a-fe24-4356-a1af-37a1d8c8cd1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Content quality criteria"}], "description": "Students learn what exists before reorganizing it."}, {"id": "f7907e50-9e9f-4905-beec-df0e02ad7b43", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Taxonomy and labeling", "children": [{"id": "14ba930b-4d3d-47cf-a4f9-b06f27b428a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Controlled vocabulary"}, {"id": "decf9802-7cd6-4196-af02-d8810787c9c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Navigation labels"}, {"id": "ca03696d-c9da-48aa-8229-adccb216735f", "type": "concept", "title": "Metadata and tags"}], "description": "The point is to name and group things in ways users understand."}, {"id": "0ae809d6-7f23-4f25-98c8-8f5bbf2d3395", "type": "subtopic", "title": "IA testing", "children": [{"id": "c730fd1a-41d9-4d33-8832-c8fe2e0256e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Card sorting"}, {"id": "17bb516a-f33c-4220-a38e-10465ad3e113", "type": "concept", "title": "Tree testing"}, {"id": "62e86b46-4ec3-4a9f-9ad6-844cc027adfe", "type": "concept", "title": "Sitemap critique"}], "description": "Students evaluate structure before committing to interface polish."}]}, {"id": "f1e7d7d9-a077-4d8a-b72f-d9dc975418b7", "type": "topic", "title": "Content Strategy, UX Writing, and Plain Language", "description": "Words are interface. This section teaches students to make content clear, helpful, inclusive, and action-oriented.", "children": [{"id": "8b6e35b0-4d47-4a5e-9de9-1a20c5ba6e83", "type": "subtopic", "title": "UX writing", "children": [{"id": "2a74463a-c3ba-4741-9ed5-81942ff82bf6", "type": "concept", "title": "Microcopy"}, {"id": "8c5b8b1f-50ef-4f23-b938-ea5d925d300f", "type": "concept", "title": "Error prevention and recovery"}, {"id": "f336167f-32d7-4fa9-bfac-792a0ff0607b", "type": "concept", "title": "Calls to action"}], "description": "Students learn to write labels, instructions, errors, and empty states that help people move forward."}, {"id": "0d82f06d-c2bb-410d-b42d-7c93c2cff3b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Plain language", "children": [{"id": "b300da9f-dd58-4779-a8eb-a5c3870b50b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Readable structure"}, {"id": "dcfbfe29-50c8-486b-8057-ecbee43026a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Short sentences and familiar words"}, {"id": "5f04c83e-041c-4a7d-a623-df04987c362d", "type": "concept", "title": "Scannable hierarchy"}], "description": "The gist is to reduce cognitive load and make content usable for more people."}, {"id": "ab8f944c-866d-4b3b-a75c-c80bac48fad0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Content governance", "children": [{"id": "9012d328-d9b8-4743-91c3-38fba93218f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Voice and tone rules"}, {"id": "9d9d817f-01a0-4336-aa62-92df104c56cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Content models"}, {"id": "bd395ab3-a4dd-42ec-807e-9015ecee2650", "type": "concept", "title": "Approval and maintenance workflows"}], "description": "Students learn how content stays consistent after launch."}]}, {"id": "6b94d948-e4a9-4c1f-81f8-b1bb12a24454", "type": "topic", "title": "Interaction Design: Flows, States, Patterns, and Feedback", "description": "Interaction design shapes product behavior. Students learn to design not just screens, but sequences, decisions, feedback, errors, and edge cases.", "children": [{"id": "d1a736eb-58f6-42c9-b7ec-b9aee009b2ee", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Task flows", "children": [{"id": "a65e514d-eaee-4892-8daf-79942466ff2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Happy paths"}, {"id": "1ab9dbea-ba6e-46aa-911e-e79883232c6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Alternate paths"}, {"id": "0befdf32-5e36-493d-b414-700fb27bd05d", "type": "concept", "title": "Failure and recovery"}], "description": "Students map how people move through a goal."}, {"id": "1b828f25-8447-47ed-ab44-f442b01f4ce3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interaction patterns", "children": [{"id": "b8498c2b-b08e-4f67-913b-98004cd53186", "type": "concept", "title": "Forms, navigation, search, filters"}, {"id": "e3fce006-a273-429f-87e0-9155657021ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Onboarding and settings"}, {"id": "d826da7e-4276-4231-8fd7-dd553be7916e", "type": "concept", "title": "Progressive disclosure"}], "description": "The point is to use familiar patterns intentionally and break them only with a reason."}, {"id": "2b48fe3b-28df-4adf-aef6-1eb5b3173047", "type": "subtopic", "title": "States and feedback", "children": [{"id": "7d580fd7-522c-4700-91ab-22056aa4664d", "type": "concept", "title": "Loading, success, error, and empty states"}, {"id": "297599b7-61fa-4289-9544-ed1e6859a153", "type": "concept", "title": "Validation and confirmation"}, {"id": "bc54c76d-da10-40e5-812a-cb7e82f5bae9", "type": "concept", "title": "Microinteractions"}], "description": "Students design for the moments between actions."}]}, {"id": "fdfb1021-f372-4298-8bf8-8a95f2736fd1", "type": "topic", "title": "Wireframing, Sketching, and Low-Fidelity Prototyping", "description": "Low-fidelity work keeps students fast and honest. The goal is to explore structure and flow before visual polish creates attachment.", "children": [{"id": "01f739bc-9018-46a3-975e-c8ffebdbd8be", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sketching", "children": [{"id": "442a5940-24fd-4afe-a573-7aef9e03786e", "type": "concept", "title": "Crazy eights and thumbnails"}, {"id": "d569b8c9-c970-4642-ae9f-123b36498ba2", "type": "concept", "title": "Screen variants"}, {"id": "1aa329df-d7a2-4a9a-a03e-7ff36452daf8", "type": "concept", "title": "Critique-ready sketches"}], "description": "Students generate multiple options quickly."}, {"id": "a9c7baa5-ee7f-4890-a2a7-d143bced8345", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Wireframes", "children": [{"id": "a7fff445-ee39-4e7b-8608-3c9482dec170", "type": "concept", "title": "Page structure"}, {"id": "cb980215-0649-4cd3-a0cb-72b0733290ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Content priority"}, {"id": "97e2a005-ea80-4013-bb05-7ab8198804ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsive considerations"}], "description": "The point is to define hierarchy, layout, and function without distracting surface detail."}, {"id": "d80c8608-6238-4500-87ee-79c351c073f6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Low-fidelity tests", "children": [{"id": "97bc2deb-4798-47ee-90d0-095e106b54f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Paper prototypes"}, {"id": "07268c8d-a44e-4a95-89a9-a7d9262cdde6", "type": "concept", "title": "Clickable wireframes"}, {"id": "bda3f9f5-d657-4d34-92b2-84850c4fbfd7", "type": "concept", "title": "Task-based feedback"}], "description": "Students learn to test concepts with lightweight prototypes."}]}, {"id": "2ae2d2e6-afd6-424e-90bd-2ce06e6cfb94", "type": "topic", "title": "High-Fidelity Prototyping, UI Detail, and Visual Hierarchy", "description": "High-fidelity prototypes communicate interaction, hierarchy, content, and visual system. Students learn to make prototypes realistic enough for evaluation and stakeholder review.", "children": [{"id": "7fafd184-b6be-4dc9-ad8a-800f59a5a52d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visual hierarchy", "children": [{"id": "f1d59bd3-57ab-4f24-8803-fe9161507bb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Typography and spacing"}, {"id": "5e214d8a-1c55-4ae0-a4f9-aba5091edede", "type": "concept", "title": "Color and emphasis"}, {"id": "bfb023f7-73d6-40e7-b881-484f8e3c1038", "type": "concept", "title": "Layout rhythm"}], "description": "Students shape attention through size, contrast, spacing, and grouping."}, {"id": "ad38ab97-10e1-4980-b74b-b14c28480a1a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prototype behavior", "children": [{"id": "8bf67bc5-48a0-4844-867a-8c20da2e4b2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Clickable flows"}, {"id": "bf48631e-ef0b-432f-a537-b73b9dd867a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Overlays and transitions"}, {"id": "50b4ac90-1447-42b6-8f82-6b62c101226d", "type": "concept", "title": "Prototype limitations"}], "description": "The gist is to represent enough interaction for meaningful testing."}, {"id": "c4cea770-6d29-44ad-9719-879b3f381648", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Responsive detail", "children": [{"id": "9897697a-72ac-4838-9ba3-0582059cc9a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Breakpoints"}, {"id": "4fbf983f-a537-48f8-b922-be3b09ac8644", "type": "concept", "title": "Touch targets"}, {"id": "c347be6e-714f-49f0-bbf9-95d76bad5e16", "type": "concept", "title": "Mobile and desktop patterns"}], "description": "Students design for different screens and contexts."}]}, {"id": "f40433f9-84dc-4e19-a773-a314329621b9", "type": "topic", "title": "Usability Testing, Heuristic Evaluation, and Iteration", "description": "Evaluation teaches students that design quality is discovered through use. They learn to observe, measure, prioritize, and revise.", "children": [{"id": "c216a61e-fe6c-4ed9-9f05-5b7cabb68ba1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Usability testing", "children": [{"id": "7983f7f1-4465-41d2-95fd-5bf19a2e60eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Test scripts"}, {"id": "4041ef2d-0a20-4f49-9d1c-b26f524b6c21", "type": "concept", "title": "Moderation and observation"}, {"id": "09eba611-c202-4528-bbf9-85f170a3b645", "type": "concept", "title": "Task success and severity"}], "description": "Students conduct task-based tests that reveal breakdowns."}, {"id": "6eeed823-b063-43e0-841c-1b838d08ae46", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Heuristic evaluation", "children": [{"id": "248aa83d-f8e4-4f74-b24e-83674d0792f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Nielsen heuristics"}, {"id": "dbae3b22-7bbf-440c-a747-8bda3d9030c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Consistency and standards"}, {"id": "8bc08b34-a320-4373-a9ec-1f8054807645", "type": "concept", "title": "Error prevention"}], "description": "The point is to use expert review as a quick but limited diagnostic tool."}, {"id": "1ddf7151-8c90-4d68-b444-7f34552c27eb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Iteration planning", "children": [{"id": "6407df5a-b5b5-4fc2-bee2-8e7b6c94b11b", "type": "concept", "title": "Prioritization matrix"}, {"id": "54f9bf46-4b6e-4179-b363-1786dee23c9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Issue tracking"}, {"id": "537a90a9-0876-4f52-9db6-7eee989d1652", "type": "concept", "title": "Before/after rationale"}], "description": "Students convert findings into design changes."}]}, {"id": "9ff3eb89-6a2b-40b4-9b1f-370b325e95e3", "type": "topic", "title": "Accessibility, WCAG, Assistive Technology, and Inclusive Design", "description": "Accessibility is treated as core UX quality. Students learn to design and evaluate for diverse bodies, senses, cognition, technologies, and contexts.", "children": [{"id": "1906376f-525a-4a7c-8ea5-566affc40dec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "WCAG foundations", "children": [{"id": "4077f496-878a-40da-8e52-c017bdfbdd09", "type": "concept", "title": "Contrast and text alternatives"}, {"id": "af7bb68a-41e3-4b44-b127-908d09ff84e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Keyboard access and focus"}, {"id": "05ce45cf-79ab-4b93-85c0-c4727d596e38", "type": "concept", "title": "Error identification and instructions"}], "description": "Students learn practical standards for perceivable, operable, understandable, and robust experiences."}, {"id": "ebf7d15a-ebe4-4d80-8582-abfad77382e4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Assistive technology awareness", "children": [{"id": "beef57dd-283a-4f87-b851-b8e51b8e0fac", "type": "concept", "title": "Screen readers"}, {"id": "bf32ad94-6339-494a-9bd6-28065aff8ae6", "type": "concept", "title": "Keyboard and switch navigation"}, {"id": "23b041a1-7443-4f77-bc4b-a90c14aebc44", "type": "concept", "title": "Zoom, captions, and voice input"}], "description": "The gist is to understand how people may use products beyond a default mouse-and-screen path."}, {"id": "f83560ac-a65e-45c3-a017-05de9df19f71", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inclusive research", "children": [{"id": "63ea572c-0f1c-4312-8fc8-6839d075b1ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible recruiting"}, {"id": "b993818b-80a9-49fe-a410-aba0892baa8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Accommodation planning"}, {"id": "c5fec824-94bf-4a9d-bc50-e9e29d5f1cb0", "type": "concept", "title": "Bias and exclusion audits"}], "description": "Students learn to include disability and difference without tokenizing participants."}]}, {"id": "d48b0c43-3713-48c3-ace0-2f08144939f5", "type": "topic", "title": "Design Systems, Components, Tokens, and Governance", "description": "Design systems help UX work scale. Students learn to connect research, interaction patterns, accessibility, visual design, and engineering handoff through reusable components.", "children": [{"id": "4b78d02e-940f-474f-b9ec-40dd37d40578", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Components and patterns", "children": [{"id": "34526dc1-459f-4ee8-b543-ca05e2ae1a6a", "type": "concept", "title": "Buttons, forms, cards, tables"}, {"id": "45c25dab-9b6c-4bdd-917e-e1c041ebae0b", "type": "concept", "title": "States and variants"}, {"id": "0e49059e-6665-4534-bb64-1567fc6718ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Pattern selection"}], "description": "Students define reusable building blocks with clear behavior."}, {"id": "3a1d8e4d-165e-4751-85ec-22622be40f60", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tokens and documentation", "children": [{"id": "e74dd159-4312-4b87-8caa-6e01ee56b731", "type": "concept", "title": "Color, type, spacing, and motion tokens"}, {"id": "ae7b0bf4-07b0-4c60-ac70-14be68428447", "type": "concept", "title": "Usage guidance"}, {"id": "6ea05369-b450-4f82-afc1-c24db7d93df4", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessibility notes"}], "description": "The point is to make design decisions implementable and maintainable."}, {"id": "603b055d-17ad-4677-bee9-0bcaba4eaba9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Governance", "children": [{"id": "2ce2833a-0a5a-492e-ac9f-b485b69952ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Contribution models"}, {"id": "ac974abe-1b69-4f86-852c-c3209ab527a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Versioning"}, {"id": "d83351a2-8203-4c0d-8932-07982121287b", "type": "concept", "title": "Design-system critique"}], "description": "Students learn how systems evolve without becoming chaotic."}]}, {"id": "61257362-fe73-4f00-9b73-fb4c310c120b", "type": "topic", "title": "Service Design, Omnichannel Journeys, and Operational Reality", "description": "Many experiences extend beyond a screen. This topic helps students connect digital UX to services, support, policies, people, and physical or social contexts.", "children": [{"id": "06685edc-ea63-4c30-9da6-9a5fdc87b303", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Service journey mapping", "children": [{"id": "cb68453a-7d7c-4e1f-bf84-33f096b24990", "type": "concept", "title": "Touchpoints"}, {"id": "af5e0c22-d1a4-4802-86ff-45d0200318cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Emotional arcs"}, {"id": "ef2dafe7-ed4f-49d6-8b4a-5bb5ad8d1436", "type": "concept", "title": "Channel transitions"}], "description": "Students map experiences across channels and time."}, {"id": "db49027a-ddb7-4d03-a4cd-9fd09373ec31", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Blueprinting operations", "children": [{"id": "08970fcc-b13c-4b07-a9d4-d3cdde28a250", "type": "concept", "title": "Frontstage and backstage"}, {"id": "f5a14d64-3d44-4bb5-a193-0b5cbb237ab6", "type": "concept", "title": "Policies and handoffs"}, {"id": "f2878540-e61c-4d05-945c-6078aa68dfa4", "type": "concept", "title": "Failure points"}], "description": "The gist is to understand what must happen behind the interface."}, {"id": "c143c766-dcc7-4d24-bc86-12184d5174a2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Omnichannel design", "children": [{"id": "5b213a57-1988-4c00-bd00-01c547f09cfe", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-channel tasks"}, {"id": "5dae6ee9-becc-4bb5-a1e3-594eb75d1a48", "type": "concept", "title": "Notifications and follow-up"}, {"id": "1853d504-193d-491a-85fb-324874493e9b", "type": "concept", "title": "Support and recovery"}], "description": "Students plan continuity across devices, places, and support channels."}]}, {"id": "acab3ae8-5448-40b5-8bce-beabf1efdbaf", "type": "topic", "title": "Ethics, Privacy, Dark Patterns, AI, and Responsible UX", "description": "UX designers shape choices and consequences. This section asks students to examine harm, privacy, manipulation, bias, and responsible design in emerging technology.", "children": [{"id": "f886722b-bb7e-4552-8d9c-1698ec8301c6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dark patterns", "children": [{"id": "8d4051fd-47fc-4ecc-b38a-2729111bc36e", "type": "concept", "title": "Forced continuity"}, {"id": "386bf063-9726-4e91-971e-26f7b1aae6a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Obstruction and misdirection"}, {"id": "a7d894f0-cb63-4bad-9346-35e150699973", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent and unsubscribe patterns"}], "description": "Students learn to recognize and avoid manipulative design."}, {"id": "fc235702-aca8-4387-9d12-9b0bd1349b25", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Privacy and trust", "children": [{"id": "afcf0f6a-26d9-4774-918d-9ce8ccb08c99", "type": "concept", "title": "Data minimization"}, {"id": "330f8fd2-0dba-4e43-8ed1-4155ddd626e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Permission flows"}, {"id": "88fefbd0-934b-43d3-bfb4-14818fb015cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparency and control"}], "description": "The point is to design data experiences people can understand and control."}, {"id": "80e2a02a-a4c7-45fd-9f7b-d947169fae70", "type": "subtopic", "title": "AI and automation", "children": [{"id": "5dbc21cc-ccd4-4acf-83b8-f5d9c344e205", "type": "concept", "title": "Human-in-the-loop decisions"}, {"id": "32b39058-f704-48d1-8e8a-83340e234d09", "type": "concept", "title": "AI disclosure"}, {"id": "7a20bb15-4f42-45a5-9911-0e9bd99f6ebf", "type": "concept", "title": "Error and uncertainty communication"}], "description": "Students consider explainability, bias, accountability, and human oversight."}]}, {"id": "6a6aaf8c-ecfb-459e-ac8e-ce39a8558951", "type": "topic", "title": "Collaboration, Critique, Handoff, and Product Team Practice", "description": "UX work is collaborative. Students learn to communicate with product managers, engineers, researchers, content designers, visual designers, and stakeholders.", "children": [{"id": "29ed9101-fbb7-4e9b-a0ab-6a2fa2b71409", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critique practice", "children": [{"id": "0f1d68e0-8e42-4807-adae-af21d36bcf11", "type": "concept", "title": "Critique prompts"}, {"id": "0681ad18-a49e-43ed-8825-558538f70fae", "type": "concept", "title": "Design rationale"}, {"id": "35c6ad26-0990-494c-bbb3-08970bc241c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Revision decisions"}], "description": "Students learn to give and receive feedback tied to goals and evidence."}, {"id": "51064cc5-4b1d-46fb-bcfd-3a5cb0514236", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Handoff", "children": [{"id": "8d9e3167-f0b5-42d5-851c-9332d58437bf", "type": "concept", "title": "Annotations"}, {"id": "5f3310d5-9b3b-4ab7-b4e3-0bebe30bed02", "type": "concept", "title": "Specs and edge cases"}, {"id": "cea3679d-3b9c-4abe-807e-db88104a8edb", "type": "concept", "title": "QA with engineering"}], "description": "The gist is to make implementation easier without pretending design ends at delivery."}, {"id": "02b31ea7-a6dd-4ef8-9a3a-75a1f568eb2a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Team rituals", "children": [{"id": "561e076e-9456-4b49-80b4-f91448f6b8ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Standups and reviews"}, {"id": "953f374b-d15d-4bc6-877d-086b983fc9fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Design sprints"}, {"id": "1bd49f60-831c-4c76-b278-844e185a979d", "type": "concept", "title": "Decision logs"}], "description": "Students practice professional workflows common in product teams."}]}, {"id": "d00087ad-19e2-4d59-a591-8e0760105093", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone: UX Case Study and Portfolio Presentation", "description": "The capstone asks students to synthesize the course into a portfolio-ready UX project. The final case study should show judgment, craft, evidence, iteration, and communication.", "children": [{"id": "fff1d036-4620-42e1-9072-29b9edc8db43", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case-study strategy", "children": [{"id": "51fe52dd-c83f-4ce7-9d5d-9248d62a9598", "type": "concept", "title": "Problem and constraints"}, {"id": "142fa734-a3b5-4de6-a571-4bcc39140866", "type": "concept", "title": "Role and collaborators"}, {"id": "6e52c857-5b93-4e18-8841-341c5213f416", "type": "concept", "title": "Process overview"}], "description": "Students choose a narrative that explains the problem and their contribution clearly."}, {"id": "bffeac2e-7a22-4a84-90db-bba4b7352682", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence and prototype", "children": [{"id": "b9322b7a-ee9f-4d06-a0d5-b4a872cd1b5b", "type": "concept", "title": "Key insights"}, {"id": "d874b4e5-5b65-45e1-b290-426da89290f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Design iterations"}, {"id": "ac1dafa1-b7b8-4a3b-bda7-5fff2d761579", "type": "concept", "title": "Final prototype and rationale"}], "description": "The point is to show how research and testing shaped the design."}, {"id": "706f97cf-d0b9-4021-9f24-f234324137a0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Presentation and reflection", "children": [{"id": "8ee7eaf0-4d14-4fbc-868e-ed3dedf1ef8e", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio writing"}, {"id": "5e08bcd5-76a9-4948-93f7-3d71e2260392", "type": "concept", "title": "Metrics and limitations"}, {"id": "0288802e-5368-4646-974d-0958fc67dcff", "type": "concept", "title": "Next iteration plan"}], "description": "Students learn to speak about tradeoffs, outcomes, and next steps like emerging professionals."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$uxdsjson$::jsonb,
